    rdfs:label "Hamilton's equations"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P12 "Q1115699" ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "Hamiltonian mechanics emerged in 1833 as a reformulation of Lagrangian mechanics. Introduced by Sir William Rowan Hamilton, Hamiltonian mechanics replaces (generalized) velocities used in Lagrangian mechanics with (generalized) momenta. Both theories provide interpretations of classical mechanics and describe the same physical phenomena." ;
