        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663> ;
    rdfs:label "Freundlich isotherm model"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "The Freundlich isotherm model is an empirical adsorption model that describes how solutes adhere to heterogeneous surfaces with varying affinities. It accounts for multilayer adsorption rather than a single uniform layer. The model is widely applied in environmental and chemical engineering to study pollutant adsorption on materials such as activated carbon, soil, and biochar." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270" ;
    mathmoddb:P147 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775714" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1560 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775720" ;
    mathmoddb:P286 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821336" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6672084" ;
    mathmoddb:P558 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q74555" ;
    schema:description "mathematical model for equilibrium adsorption of solutes on heterogeneous surfaces"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775714> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247> ;
    rdfs:label "linear parameter estimation (Freundlich isotherm)"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This task performs linear parameter estimation using experimental adsorption equilibrium data. The objective is to determine the Freundlich capacity and adsorption intensity constants by fitting the linearized Freundlich equation to measured solute concentration and adsorbed amount data. The results characterize the adsorption capacity and surface heterogeneity of the adsorbent." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
