    mathmoddb:P989 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>E</mi><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>50</mn></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>H</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    schema:description "sigmoidal dose–response equation describing cooperative effects"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775839> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247> ;
    rdfs:label "nonlinear parameter estimation (Hill dose-response model)"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This task performs nonlinear parameter estimation using dose–response data based on the Hill dose–response model. It estimates the maximal system response, the half-maximal concentration, and the cooperativity exponent by fitting the nonlinear sigmoidal Hill equation directly to observed concentration–effect measurements. Nonlinear regression eliminates distortions from linear transformations and yields robust estimates across a wide range of cooperative behaviors. The resulting parameters describe drug efficacy, potency, and the steepness of the dose–response relationship. This approach is widely used in pharmacology, toxicology, and pharmacokinetic–pharmacodynamic modeling." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1560 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775854" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6672087" ;
    mathmoddb:P558 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q3116516" ;
    schema:description "nonlinear estimation of Hill dose–response model parameters"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775840> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663> ;
    rdfs:label "Emax model"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "The Emax model in its non-cooperative form is a pharmacodynamic dose–response model that describes how drug effect increases with concentration in a simple hyperbolic manner. It assumes no cooperativity in the system, meaning the Hill coefficient is fixed at one, producing a non-sigmoidal saturation curve. The model is characterized by a maximal achievable effect and the concentration that produces half of this maximum, offering intuitive measures of drug efficacy and potency. As the n = 1 specialization of the Hill dose-response model, it represents the simplest form of saturable concentration–effect behavior. This non-cooperative Emax model is widely used in pharmacology, toxicology, and pharmacokinetic–pharmacodynamic analyses when dose–response relationships do not exhibit sigmoidal characteristics." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270" ;
    mathmoddb:P147 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775842" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1560 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775841" ;
    mathmoddb:P286 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775861" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775551" ;
    schema:description "non-cooperative hyperbolic dose–response model"@en .

