<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6820970> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663> ;
    rdfs:label "Kiselev isotherm model"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "The Kiselev isotherm model describes adsorption occurring in a localized monomolecular layer, where adsorbate molecules may form surface complexes with one another. Unlike the Langmuir model, Kiselev explicitly includes a complex-formation parameter that accounts for associations between adsorbed molecules at neighboring sites. This allows the model to represent cooperative or associative adsorption behavior on heterogeneous or interacting surfaces. It is used primarily to interpret adsorption on solids where pairwise interactions or dimer formation occurs. Applications include surface chemistry, catalysis, and environmental adsorption processes such as chemical wastewater treatment." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270" ;
    mathmoddb:P147 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6820972" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1560 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6820976" ;
    mathmoddb:P286 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775858" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775551" ;
    mathmoddb:P558 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6820992" ;
    schema:description "adsorption model for localized monolayer with complex formation"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6820971> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247> ;
    rdfs:label "nonlinear parameter estimation (Kiselev model)"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This task performs nonlinear parameter estimation using adsorption equilibrium data to determine the Kiselev equilibrium constant and the complex formation constant. The nonlinear Kiselev equation is fitted directly to coverage and concentration values to capture the formation of complexes between adsorbed molecules. The results quantify adsorption affinity and the strength of lateral associative interactions. This method avoids potential distortions caused by linearization." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1560 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6820976" ;
