<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821250> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247> ;
    rdfs:label "nonlinear parameter estimation (Khan model)"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This task estimates the parameters of the Khan isotherm model by nonlinear regression using equilibrium adsorption data. Experimental measurements of equilibrium adsorbed amount and equilibrium concentration are fitted to the Khan equation to determine the maximum adsorption capacity, affinity constant, and heterogeneity exponent. The fitting process minimizes the deviation between observed and predicted adsorption values across the concentration range. The resulting parameters characterize adsorption capacity, surface affinity, and heterogeneity of the adsorbent. This task is commonly applied in adsorption studies of aqueous pollutants and organic solutes." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1560 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821242" ;
    mathmoddb:P1684 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775714" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247" ;
    schema:description "nonlinear fitting of Khan isotherm parameters"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821251> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663> ;
    rdfs:label "Khan isotherm model"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "The Khan isotherm model is a generalized adsorption isotherm developed to describe equilibrium adsorption in dilute solutions. It unifies the Langmuir and Freundlich models within a single mathematical framework by introducing a model exponent that controls surface heterogeneity. At a specific parameter limit, the model reduces to the Langmuir isotherm, while at high equilibrium concentrations it approaches Freundlich-type behavior. The model is applicable to single-component adsorption and was originally formulated to support extensions to multicomponent systems. It is widely used in environmental and chemical engineering studies of aqueous adsorption." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270" ;
    mathmoddb:P147 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821250" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1560 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821249" ;
    mathmoddb:P1684 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775766" ;
    mathmoddb:P286 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775858" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6672110" ;
    schema:description "generalized Langmuir–Freundlich adsorption isotherm"@en .

