<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821297> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
    rdfs:label "heat unit factor"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "The heat unit factor expresses the relative progress of crop development on a normalized scale from zero to one. It is derived from the accumulated heat unit index using a crop-specific sigmoid function. HUF is used to regulate phenology-dependent growth processes. It provides a smooth, continuous representation of crop development stage." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237" ;
    schema:description "normalized crop development factor"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821298> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
    rdfs:label "heat unit response shape parameters"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "These crop-specific parameters determine the shape and steepness of the sigmoid relationship between heat unit index and heat unit factor. They are computed by fitting the heat unit factor equation to two predefined calibration points. The parameters remain constant throughout the simulation. They reflect phenological characteristics specific to each crop." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237" ;
    schema:description "shape parameters of HUF sigmoid curve"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821299> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
    rdfs:label "accumulated potential biomass"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This quantity represents the cumulative dry matter biomass produced by a crop under potential growth conditions. It is obtained by summing daily potential biomass increments over time. The value reflects the maximum attainable biomass prior to stress reduction and partitioning. It serves as the basis for modeling structural development and yield formation." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775552" ;
    schema:description "total potential crop dry matter"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821301> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
    rdfs:label "solar radiation"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P12 "Q17996169" ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1684 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821281" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775552" ;
    schema:description "electromagnetic radiation received from the Sun"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821302> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183> ;
    rdfs:label "daylength calculation equation"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This equation computes the length of daylight as a function of geographic latitude and the Sun’s declination angle. It is based on astronomical relationships describing Earth–Sun geometry over the annual cycle. Daylength varies seasonally and with latitude, influencing available solar radiation and crop growth potential. The equation provides a deterministic estimate of photoperiod for each simulation day. Daylength is later used to modulate potential biomass production." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775550" ;
    mathmoddb:P983 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    mathmoddb:P989 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>H</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mn>7.64</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#x2061;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>360</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#x2061;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>0.044</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#x2061;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>360</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#x2061;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo></mrow></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    schema:description "computes daylength from latitude and solar declination"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821303> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183> ;
    rdfs:label "solar declination angle equation"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This equation computes the solar declination angle for a given simulation day based on Earth’s orbital position. The declination angle represents the angular displacement of the Sun relative to Earth’s equatorial plane and varies periodically over the year. Its seasonal variation is driven by Earth’s axial tilt and revolution around the Sun. The formulation approximates this variation using a sinusoidal function of the day index. The resulting solar declination angle is used in astronomical calculations of daylength and solar radiation geometry." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775550" ;
    mathmoddb:P983 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>S</mi><mi>D</mi></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    mathmoddb:P989 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mn>0.4102</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#x2061;</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>365</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>80.25</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo></mrow></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    schema:description "determine solar declination angle on a specific day"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821304> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534237> ;
    rdfs:label "leaf area index"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P12 "Q446746" ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "Leaf area index is a dimensionless measure of canopy size defined as leaf area per unit ground area. It controls the fraction of incoming radiation intercepted by the canopy. Higher values correspond to denser canopies and greater light interception. Leaf area index is a dynamic state variable determined by crop growth and development." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534271" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1684 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821294" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6672114" ;
    schema:description "dimensionless quantity that characterizes plant canopies"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821305> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183> ;
    rdfs:label "start of leaf area decline assumption"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183" ;
    mathmoddb:P983 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    mathmoddb:P989 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    schema:description "assumption defining the start of leaf area decline in terms of heat unit index"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821306> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183> ;
    rdfs:label "heat unit factor equation"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This equation computes the heat unit factor as a sigmoid function of the heat unit index. The heat unit factor represents normalized crop developmental progress from emergence to maturity. Its functional form ensures slow development during early and late stages and more rapid change during intermediate stages. Crop-specific parameters determine the shape of the sigmoid relationship and are calibrated using predefined pairs of heat unit index and heat unit factor values. The resulting heat unit factor is used to control phenology-dependent processes such as leaf area development and biomass partitioning." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6672094" ;
    mathmoddb:P983 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>I</mi></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    mathmoddb:P989 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">⋅</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    schema:description "computes phenological development factor from heat units"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821307> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183> ;
    rdfs:label "potential biomass accumulation equation"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This equation updates the accumulated potential crop biomass by adding the daily potential biomass increment to its previous value. It represents the temporal integration of daily biomass production over the growing season. The formulation assumes that biomass accumulation is additive and does not impose additional physiological constraints beyond those governing daily production. The equation is applied at each simulation time step to maintain the biomass state variable. It provides the accumulated potential biomass used in subsequent allocation and yield formation processes." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775550" ;
    mathmoddb:P983 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    mathmoddb:P989 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">+</mo><mi>Δ</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    schema:description "accumulates daily potential crop biomass"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821310> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183> ;
    rdfs:label "potential leaf area development equation"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This equation computes the daily change in leaf area index during the active canopy development phase of crop growth. It applies from crop emergence until the onset of leaf decline and determines the rate at which leaf area expands. The formulation links leaf area development to phenological progress through the heat unit factor while limiting growth as the canopy approaches a crop-specific maximum leaf area index. Crop stress effects are incorporated through a regulating factor that reduces leaf expansion under unfavorable conditions. The equation ensures gradual and biologically realistic canopy expansion prior to senescence." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6672094" ;
    mathmoddb:P983 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    mathmoddb:P989 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">⋅</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><msqrt><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>R</mi><mi>E</mi><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    schema:description "computes daily increase in leaf area index"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821311> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183> ;
    rdfs:label "leaf area index equation"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This equation represents the dynamic update of leaf area index during the crop growing season. Leaf area index is treated as a state variable that evolves daily as a result of leaf expansion and senescence processes. From crop emergence to the onset of leaf decline, leaf area index is updated by adding a computed daily increment. After the start of leaf decline, leaf area index is reduced according to a phenology-dependent senescence formulation. Together, the governing equations ensure biologically realistic canopy development by allowing growth, saturation, and decline of leaf area." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1674 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821305" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6672094" ;
    mathmoddb:P983 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    mathmoddb:P989 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">{</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd class=\"mwe-math-columnalign-l\"><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">+</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd class=\"mwe-math-columnalign-l\"><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class=\"mwe-math-columnalign-l\"><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo></mrow><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd class=\"mwe-math-columnalign-l\"><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">≥</mo><mi>H</mi><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>o</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo fence=\"true\" stretchy=\"true\" symmetric=\"true\" data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\"></mo></mrow></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    schema:description "dynamic canopy leaf area index over growing season"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821312> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183> ;
    rdfs:label "radiation interception equation"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This equation estimates the amount of photosynthetically active radiation intercepted by a crop canopy using Beer’s law. Incoming solar radiation is converted to photosynthetically active radiation by applying a fixed fraction. The fraction of radiation intercepted by the canopy is modeled as an exponential function of leaf area index. The extinction coefficient represents average light attenuation within the canopy. This formulation links canopy structure directly to available energy for potential biomass production." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P286 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821308" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6672094" ;
    mathmoddb:P983 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    mathmoddb:P989 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    schema:description "estimation of photosynthetically active radiation following Beer's law"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821313> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q96183> ;
    rdfs:label "potential biomass growth equation"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This equation estimates the daily potential increase in crop biomass using a radiation use efficiency approach. It follows the formulation proposed by Monteith, relating intercepted photosynthetically active radiation to dry matter production. Biomass accumulation is adjusted by a factor accounting for daylength and its daily change. The conversion efficiency parameter represents the crop-specific ability to transform radiant energy into biomass. The equation assumes optimal growing conditions without water or nutrient stress." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q5981696" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P286 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821309" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775550" ;
    mathmoddb:P983 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>Δ</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    mathmoddb:P989 "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" class=\"mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mi>Δ</mi><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">=</mo><mn>0.001</mn><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">+</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mstyle></mrow></math>" ;
    schema:description "estimates daily potential crop biomass increase following Monteith"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821314> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534247> ;
    rdfs:label "computation of potential crop biomass growth"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This task computes the potential accumulation of crop biomass based on intercepted photosynthetically active radiation and phenological development. It represents the upper bound of biomass growth achievable under optimal radiation conditions, prior to the application of biomass-reducing stresses such as water or nutrient limitation. The task integrates astronomical calculations, phenological scaling, and canopy development to determine daily potential biomass increments. Leaf area development is influenced by crop stress, but biomass conversion itself follows a radiation use efficiency approach. The resulting potential biomass provides the basis for subsequent structural development and yield formation tasks." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534272" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1560 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821357" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775549" ;
    schema:description "calculating stress-free crop biomass accumulation"@en .

<https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821315> a owl:NamedIndividual,
        <https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q68663> ;
    rdfs:label "potential crop growth model (biomass)"@en ;
    mathmoddb:P1459 "This model determines crop biomass production assuming no limitations from water, nutrients, pests, or diseases. Growth is driven by intercepted solar radiation and a crop-specific radiation use efficiency parameter. The model represents the maximum achievable growth rate under prevailing weather conditions. Phenological development controls the timing and partitioning of growth but does not constrain resource availability. The resulting biomass represents potential growth against which stress effects are later applied." ;
    mathmoddb:P1460 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534270" ;
    mathmoddb:P147 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821314" ;
    mathmoddb:P1495 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6534265" ;
    mathmoddb:P1560 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821358" ;
    mathmoddb:P286 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6821276" ;
    mathmoddb:P31 "https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/entity/Q6775551" ;
    schema:description "radiation-driven crop biomass production under optimal conditions"@en .

